WEBVTT

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:40.160
July 24th: One month has passed since we were pleasantly faced with the result of the Comic Festival drawing.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:47.420
How is the doujinshi production progressing three days
before the printing deadline, you ask?

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:55.380
The first emergency <i>the Comifes script
isn't ready at all</i> meeting is now in session.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.580
Where's Kuchiki-kun?

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.660
He said he had to go to the bathroom.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:01:59.720
He probably ran away.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:04.390
Due to certain circumstances,
I, Madarame, will chair this meeting.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:10.020
At the moment, we only have Ogiue-san's contribution of two pages.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:15.780
Let's set the reason for the delay aside for the
time being and decide on what we're going to do.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:19.620
First of all, what's the outlook on the original manga?

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.240
Will it be difficult to finish?

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.800
If it needs to be done within three days, yes.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:34.290
It isn't impossible if we extend the
deadline and pay an additional fee,

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:35.840
but that only buys us so much time.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.050
There's a five percent increase every three days, huh?

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:42.380
This isn't an issue about whether we can afford the surcharge.

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:45.600
There's no point in extending the
deadline if we don't even want to do it.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.600
I-It's as he said.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.310
W-What do you think, Kugayama-san?

00:02:53.590 --> 00:03:01.030
T-That aside, i-isn't there a l-logical problem with
having a leader who doesn't know how to draw anything?

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:02.980
<i>Uh-oh...</i>

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:07.160
Well, well, well, well...
Let's put that behind us!

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:12.380
P-People are being f-forced to do what t-they're told.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:16.180
Well, the actual quantity of work isn't excessive by any means.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.160
The majority of the work was going to be adapted from the sketchbook,

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.710
so we only needed a few pages of original content at most.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:25.020
Didn't I say you could draw
whatever you'd like, Kugayama-san?

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:30.350
Well, have you learned your
lesson on how tough reality can be?

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.090
If you have, we'll leave it at that.

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:36.330
Please draw whatever you'd like, Kugayama-san.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.400
I-Is that okay?

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.980
They say a work of passion will distinguish itself.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.610
You have to enjoy what you're doing.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.950
I-I want it to sell, though.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:49.160
Do you really want to draw Yamada, Kugayama-san?

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:53.620
Yeah, but in terms of market popularity, the president would be a better choice.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.260
L-Let me think about the plot.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:08.350
Okay. Will you be able to meet
with me as soon as the plot is finished?

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:13.020
S-Sure. It really sounds like we're in the i-industry.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:18.330
Is the same time, same place next week okay with you?

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:18.820
Yeah.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:22.400
Oh, give me a call if anything comes up.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.740
We'll take care of all the miscellaneous
work and adjust our schedule around yours.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:41.180
No offense, but I didn't expect you to be
capable of these kinds of illustrations, Ogiue-san.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:43.260
Thanks.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:44.820
Do you need me to make any adjustments?

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:48.290
This is more than enough. I'll take it.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:49.910
How's Kugayama-san doing?

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:53.030
I was supposed to meet with him today,

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:56.480
but he sounded depressed when I called him yesterday.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.800
I wonder if he ran out of ideas.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:03.440
Speaking of which, he just sent me a text message.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.330
Is something wrong?

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:08.950
It looks like he's busy.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.920
Kugayama-san?

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:11.990
Yeah.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.960
I wonder if he'll be all right.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:25.330
Yes, yes. Yes. Oh, right.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:28.260
It can't be helped, can it?

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.970
S-Sorry.

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:36.130
It's okay. The doujinshi is important,
but it's nothing compared to finding a job.

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:39.080
Well, we still have some time left.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.360
Sorry.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:45.110
If the schedule works out for you, Kugayama-san,

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:47.910
I'd like to proceed with the
scanning of the sketchbook in advance.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.700
Will you be away from your
home when you go to the interviews?

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.020
Y-Yeah.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:56.510
I guess I can't come over and do it myself, can I?

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:59.000
Well, I'm n-not sure about that.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.150
That's okay. We can still make up for lost time.

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:06.040
More importantly, good luck with the job interviews.

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:06.970
Okay.

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:10.810
I guess that means we'll have less time to work with.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:13.510
I think we can make something out of it, though.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.930
I should extend the deadline.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:31.010
What? You're kidding me.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.460
I can't focus on what I'm trying to do for some reason.

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:42.800
Is this it?

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:48.890
It's more difficult for me to work without a goal in mind.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.100
What should we do?

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.830
W-Why don't you write something, S-Sasahara?

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:03.000
T-There's not much time left.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.590
I-I'm not sure how long it'll take me to c-come up with a plot.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:10.450
A b-basic idea would be enough.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.160
No way, I can't do it.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:17.140
I-It's pretty unreasonable to give up without even a-attempting it.

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:18.160
But...

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.710
C-Come on.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.880
Okay. Is there a general idea I should keep in mind?

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:28.770
Y-You can write whatever you'd like.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.800
Kugayama-san, you're the one who has to draw it.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:36.190
I-I'll work with whatever you c-come up with, Sasahara.

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:39.730
T-That might turn out b-better, actually.

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:41.370
I see.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:43.510
I'll do my best.

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:44.850
O-Okay.

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:48.700
I know things haven't been going as
well as we hoped, but please do your best.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.200
We're depending on you,
Kugayama-san.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:59.080
In other words, Chihiro snuck into the student
council room,
but the president suddenly came back.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:04.180
Right. He hides inside the cabinet and
watches as the president starts to change.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:06.590
The story starts from there.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:09.430
It might be a little too stereotypical.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.210
What do you think?

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:19.610
T-To be honest, i-it feels like something's missing.

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:24.040
W-Well, in terms of a premise,
there's e-enough room for development,

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:27.510
but I don't see a reason to draw this as it is.

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:45.470
Enomoto Chihiro.

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:49.480
Ouch...

00:08:56.900 --> 00:09:00.360
Look carefully, Chihiro-chan.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:03.850
I love you.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.390
Has this been rejected as well?

00:09:08.390 --> 00:09:12.520
No, it's just something I can't draw.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:15.400
In other words, it's not even worth the effort.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.520
Y-Yeah.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:23.000
Well, h-how should I put this?
I'd personally like Yamada to be involved.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:31.060
You should have drawn that from the beginning!

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:35.280
Am I wrong?

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:36.680
A typical conflict of interests, isn't it?

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:37.740
Kousaka-san!

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:41.470
W-Well, I admit that was my fault.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:47.890
H-However, I'm trying to s-say
something more f-fundamental than that.

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:51.300
I-It's like there's a difference in opinion between us.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:54.900
What's that?

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.280
Are you trying to say you were never interested in doing it?

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:01.990
No, I l-lost interest as time passed.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:07.290
Was that because of me?

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:34.400
Is everything my fault?

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.270
T-That's not it.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:37.780
I...

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:43.700
W-Well, ultimately, I-I'm responsible for everything, right?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.600
That can't be helped!

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:50.950
You're the only one who can draw and has access to a scanner and Photoshop!

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:53.730
Didn't I say I-I was busy?

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:56.010
I have graduation papers and job interviews to take care of.

00:10:56.010 --> 00:11:00.260
T-Tanaka's going to a v-vocational school for apparel.

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:04.810
M-Madarame is... doing whatever he's doing.

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:07.220
<i>Whatever, he says...</i>

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.940
I want to graduate!

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:15.880
I told you I'd do all the miscellaneous work, including the scanning of the sketchbook,

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:18.900
so you could concentrate on
drawing the manga, Kugayama-san.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.910
Wasn't that good enough for you?

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:30.410
If there's been a difference in opinion, it hasn't been me
who's become more assertive, but you who's lost interest.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:35.210
Th-That's the same thing.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:38.340
No, there's a difference in the degree of accountability.

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:44.010
Well!

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:45.660
Well, well, well...

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:49.270
Well, well, well... Let's put the past behind us for now.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.630
Let's leave it at that. Let's leave it at that, okay?

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:53.970
Let's focus on the future! The future!

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:57.720
We need to figure out how to overcome this predicament and decide whether we're going to make the book or not.

00:11:57.720 --> 00:12:00.750
If we are, how are we going to do it?

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:01.680
How's that?

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:08.240
It'd be d-dishonest to f-feature
sketchbook material and charge for it.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.620
W-Wouldn't it be better if we didn't publish anything?

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.440
You might be right.

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:15.470
There's no way a bunch of sketches would sell anyway.

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:18.530
Yeah, I don't know what I was thinking
when I thought we'd sell two hundred copies.

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:28.540
U-Um... well...

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:32.530
Do you want me to write something?

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:36.840
It would be a waste if we didn't do
anything after winning the Comifes drawing.

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:45.090
No, it's okay.

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:49.440
You've already done more than enough for us, Ogiue-san.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.650
I won't allow Ogiue-san to make
up for someone else's shortcomings.

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:55.870
I can't allow it. It wouldn't be right!

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.570
You don't have to do anything else.

00:12:57.570 --> 00:12:59.050
Is that so?

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:03.590
Now that it's come to this, here's what we should do.

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:08.280
If you're going to complain about dishonesty,
failing to meet a deadline is even more dishonest.

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:12.420
The least you could do is let me scan the sketchbook.

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:14.810
You don't have to write the manga anymore.

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:23.740
D-Discouraging a m-manga artist is
about the worst thing an e-editor could do,

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:28.240
n-not that we're real m-manga artists or e-editors.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:29.160
You know...

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:35.030
S-Sasahara, you're beginning to sound like Haraguchi.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:41.400
Haven't you gone too far?

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:44.050
I-I don't think I have.

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:47.420
I've noticed it, too.

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:48.890
W-What?

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:57.850
This is why you'll never be a manga artist, Kugayama-san.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:02.820
I said I was looking for a job!

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:04.430
Isn't that a convenient excuse?

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:07.160
You never wanted to become one!

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:09.440
You just wanted to salvage what was left of your pride...

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:27.580
Sasahara, let me see the schedule.

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:30.040
Sure.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:37.820
Sasahara, Kugayama, Ogiue,

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:44.850
complete a ten page manga by July 30th.

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:49.640
Oh, if they can do that, there'll only be a five percent surcharge.

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:52.500
There's only one week left.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:56.110
We weren't able to do anything in a
month, so a week's out of the question!

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:59.230
That's because you guys wasted time doing nothing, right?

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:02.070
During this next week, this is all you're going to be doing.

00:15:02.070 --> 00:15:04.370
The three of you will work on the art and story.

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:06.830
Whatever you decide on, come up with ten pages of it.

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:12.150
I'm telling you to take responsibility.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:19.710
This page can be divided into three panels.

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:21.750
Move this line over here.

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:23.480
Oh, I see.

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:28.500
The "Chihiro-chan..." line will make a bigger impact if it's on a larger panel.

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.790
That layout makes sense.

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:33.740
Hey, what else should I scan from the sketchbook?

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.200
Oh, let's see.

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:43.510
Please have a drink.

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:50.160
I'm flattered. It's an honor to be served by Ohno-san.

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:51.850
There's no need to feel that way.

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:54.920
It's a small token of appreciation for
letting us borrow your precious equipment.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.210
How are things going?

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.350
Not too well?

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:07.050
Tell Sasayan and Kugapii what I'm about to say.

00:16:07.970 --> 00:16:10.170
Don't sleep for the next three days.

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:11.990
Um, okay...

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:16.780
Ogiue, make sure you go back to
your room and get plenty of sleep.

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:22.860
Should I take over?

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:26.070
No, I just need to finish this.

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:32.380
What did Kasukabe-san have to say?

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:34.780
She told everyone not to sleep for the next three days.

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.390
W-What?

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:41.740
The provisions regiment has returned!

00:16:41.740 --> 00:16:45.960
I've successfully acquired several special hamburger lunch boxes!

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:52.490
You got what you deserved, minions of the Federation.

00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:59.460
See, it's pounding.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:06.790
It's getting so...

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:29.990
Ogiue-san?

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:45.820
I'll go get a blanket or something.

00:17:45.820 --> 00:17:48.260
It's all right, I'm already awake.

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:51.580
It won't be long until we're done, so you can go home.

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:52.710
I'm okay.

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:54.670
Are you sure?

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:57.280
I'm just going to wash my face.

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:58.620
S-Sure.

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:13.570
I'm going to conduct a mandatory check.
Please wait.

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:14.600
Okay.

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:21.250
<i>I can't believe she's looking at it,</i>

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:23.910
<i>not that I drew any of it myself.</i>

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:28.130
You awake?

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:32.600
Oh, they actually managed to finish.

00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:34.940
Yes. They're at the printing company.

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:37.090
Sasahara-senpai and Madarame-senpai, I mean.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:38.710
What about Kugayama?

00:18:38.710 --> 00:18:41.470
He gave it everything he had
last night, so he's probably still asleep.

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:43.960
Without even a minute to spare.

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:47.420
I told you it was a lame circle, didn't I?

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:50.820
It's better to keep your expectations low.

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:53.360
I never had any from the beginning.

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:55.780
Oh, is that so?

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.700
Nice doing business with you.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:03.420
As they say, all's well that ends well.

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:06.160
We still need to worry about the Comifes itself.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:11.060
When's the book going to be ready?

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:16.930
The printing company will deliver
them directly to the Comifes venue,

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:18.990
so you guys will have to wait until then.

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:20.720
It'll be on August 15th.

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:23.200
Is that how it works?

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:25.180
Do I have to go there to see it?

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:29.860
Well, we'll bring back a few copies for ourselves.

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:33.140
Sasahara-san already mentioned that a number of times!

00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:35.660
Well, I wasn't listening because I wasn't interested.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:40.320
Oh, by the way, can you really draw erotic
stuff without having any personal experience?

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:43.710
You've never really seen it yourself, right?

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:46.010
What are you trying to say?

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:51.280
No, you're supposed to ask, "What is it that I haven't seen?"

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:54.920
I have a general idea of things from looking at doujinshi.

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:59.170
I think there's something very wrong with that

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:00.470
in more ways than one.

00:20:05.130 --> 00:20:06.540
How does it look?

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:11.810
The ceremony version's definitely better than the rest.

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:16.150
The bulkier outfits aren't suitable for vendors,

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:18.710
but it feels a little awkward without a blade.

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:21.980
It's a good thing I chose that fabric.

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:26.300
That outfit isn't for me, is it?

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:29.660
Oh, I was asked to make it and I couldn't refuse.

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:31.580
What about the Tokino outfit?

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:33.460
I already made that.

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:37.040
Are you making another one for somebody else?

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:42.040
Well, it's nothing urgent. It's for the Streetfes anyway.

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:44.760
I see.

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:48.420
Will this kind of display do the job?

00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:54.840
Wouldn't two price tags give the
impression that we're selling two different titles?

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.610
Hey, aren't we going to
the ocean this year?

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:02.240
It looks like everyone's too busy thinking about other things.

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:05.030
I meant the two of us...

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:08.580
Who will be the three to claim the circle tickets?

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:11.730
What about the entrance queue?

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:13.020
Should we do it?

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:17.170
Let's have Kuchiki-kun take
care of the shameless self-promotion.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:18.880
Leave it to me!

00:23:06.750 --> 00:23:12.670
What determines which anime songs are acceptable for singing while drinking with ordinary people?

00:23:12.670 --> 00:23:14.710
Well, I don't think any song would be appropriate.

00:23:14.710 --> 00:23:16.550
That's not true!

00:23:19.650 --> 00:23:22.270
Is Eva and Sailor Moon okay?

00:23:22.270 --> 00:23:23.970
It depends on the occasion.

00:23:23.970 --> 00:23:25.750
Keroro and Negima might be okay.

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:31.950
Songs that definitely wouldn't be acceptable right

00:23:31.950 --> 00:23:33.330
What the hell is that?
